[metadata]
Name:Rules pilot NNN - Heliod stops being a creature first
Goal:Survive
Turns:1
Difficulty:Hard
Description:You are at 2 life and control Heliod, God of the Sun (a creature while your devotion to white is 5 or more), Divinity of Pride, Memnite and Phyrexian Altar, with {C}{C}{W} in your mana pool. The opponent controls Harsh Mentor. End the turn alive at 2 life with a Cleric token and Memnite on your battlefield.
Rule:rulesguru-d2fe449354030495 | Harsh Mentor looks at the source when the ability has been activated, after its costs are paid (CR 601.2i, 602.2b); sacrificing Divinity of Pride to Phyrexian Altar for the mana drops your devotion below 5, so Heliod is not a creature and Mentor does not trigger (a mana ability never triggers it, CR 605.1a)
